title DAHL-J11r3 — the signed council travels as Bron, tie-free offline
prompt Continue the 1024-round itinerary Lindy-first crux-first; send each finished increment as its own signed round; STOP at custody gates.
think r1 (odd quorum) and r2 (signed ballots) landed and sent. r3 is the Bron travel round, mirroring skate_group_bron. Agent-doable — demo seeds only, no custody crossed.
think A council loads a sky, so the record must carry the sky's shape (galaxy/star/planet counts) beside the id and size, else a recipient cannot re-seat the council. Chose a council line `council <id> <galaxies> <stars> <planets> <size>` and one `ballot <seat> <proposal> <yea> <sig-hex>` line each; the token buffer grew to six for the council line.
think rebuild reconstructs the Sky from the carried counts, re-seats through r1's load (inheriting NotAFractalLevel/EvenCouncil), and replays each ballot through r2's vote_signed — so a hand-authored record naming the compass sky's even d60 (12 5 12 60) refuses EvenCouncil on rebuild: the tie-free law travels with the record, a crux distinct from skate_group's (whose rule had no shape to carry).
think Kept the flat-Bron hex + tokenizer idiom; parse_yea accepts strictly 0 or 1 (else BadInt). still_quorum_honest re-verifies via r2 verify_ballot with the carried size; the round-trip asserts byte-for-byte equality and that 2*quorum > size survives the crossing.
obs GREEN first pass; TAME bans + width clean; r1 and r2 re-run GREEN (additive). The even-body-cannot-rebuild case is the round's honest distinction — the record carries not just votes but the shape they were cast under, and the shape is re-checked.
